[00:23.10]Here with us are aged ones,
[00:28.88]Those whose youth has passed.
[00:36.90]Here among us they endure;
[00:43.42]Still they’re holding fast.
[00:51.44]Loss of strength besets them all;
[00:58.64]Loss of mates for some.
[01:05.15]Father, please confirm their faith
[01:13.28]In the life to come.
[01:20.70](Chorus)
[01:20.85]Father, you remember
[01:25.34]How in faith they’ve run.
[01:35.04]Give them your assurance;
[01:40.10]May they hear, “Well done!”
[02:36.40]Splendid is gray-headedness
[02:39.66]Found in ways of right.
[02:42.10]Beautiful are faithful ones
[02:45.35]In Jehovah’s sight.
[02:47.39]May we always recognize
[02:50.10]They were once young too.
[02:52.82]Loyally they gave their best
[02:56.07]When their strength was new.
[02:59.04](Chorus)
[02:59.19]Father, you remember
[03:01.50]How in faith they’ve run.
[03:06.10]Give them your assurance;
[03:13.56]May they hear, “Well done!”
